{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:244d462af3572798","name":"DE Training Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-244d462af3572798","title":"DE Training Droid","revision":24099,"timestamp":"2024-10-20T15:51:45Z","sha256":"1f14cafd652631b57f3385d5a275eb6bbf33dd93d8e43fb409c15e4f7cd3134c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24099","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=DE%20Training%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-244d462af3572798","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scavenger's Guide to Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scavenger%27s_Guide_to_Droids"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The galaxy can be a dangerous place, and the one thing the rich are always looking to buy is security. Trang Robotics' Duelist Elite Training Droid is a refined, knowledgeable opponent in the art of fencing. It also makes an excellent addition to household staff and is a great conversation piece for a grand ball. This durable Droid comes standard with durasteel-alloy construction so you won't have to hold back as you progress from cautious novice to master swashbuckler. The Duelist Elite comes preprogrammed with rapier, epee, and saber dueling programs. Other programs are available from the manufacturer. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trang Robotics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trang_Robotics?action=edit&redlink=1"}," is not liable for any damage caused by reprogrammed Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["DE Training Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["The Droid From Laman"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["DE Droids are a luxury purchase, and I usually don't go out of my way to carry them. Do not misunderstand me, my friend- a Duelist Elite is a quality Droid. It is a good hand-to-hand combatant and an excellent training tool, and it makes a good impression when you make an entrance with one of these Droids at your side. But who really needs to spend their credits on something like this, eh?"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["I've dealt with a Duelist Elite only once, and that was as a customer rather than a product. QX-73 walked into my shop looking to buy a pair of Droids- a Protocol and an Astromech. I showed it a few models, mostly to humor it. Such a funny little Droid. Normally, if a Droid is sent to purchase other Droids, it is given credits or a credit authorization from its master. But this Duelist Elite tried to trade me what it called a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},". I think the Droid believed it was a Jedi! If that poor delusional thing is still out there somewhere, it needs a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Memory Wipe"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Memory_Wipe"}," as soon as possible."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["-",{"tag":"a","children":["Raalo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Raalo?action=edit&redlink=1"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Playing a DE Training Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The Duelist Elite is a Droid of the rich and is programmed as such. Although they are not as well versed in etiquette as Protocol Droids, they are expected to be proper servants- polite, well spoken, and unobtrusive. The Duelist Elite was built to help its master improve his or her combat skills, and it also generally takes on duties as head of the household servants if these Droids need a voice for their desires. Willingly or otherwise, the DE Droid often becomes a leader among Droids.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When creating a DE Training Droid hero, consider taking levels in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," to specialize in close combat and melee weapons. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," Heroic Class also has a few ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," worth looking into. The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Melee Duelist Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Melee_Duelist_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:408cbcde0c5bdc3f"}," from the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]}," is one obvious choice.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Lightsaber Sparring Partner"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Some Jedi come from wealthy families that still support them when they take up the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},", providing improved equipment and training to the sons and daughters who join the Order. Modifying a DE Droid to teach ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," combat styles is rare but not unheard of. ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trang Robotics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trang_Robotics?action=edit&redlink=1"}," donated one to the Jedi Council on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"},", but Master ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mace Windu"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mace_Windu","referenceId":"reference:95ecd6d4c9449681"}," felt that part of learning control of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," was learning how to fight without going all out, a level of control unnecessary when sparring with a Duelist Elite.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Fighting with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," is much different from fighting with a fencing weapon. The Droid must be reprogrammed with the basics of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"}," techniques, which requires a DC 11 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check and a training module that costs 1,000 credits. If the reprogramming is successful, the Droid gains the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Lightsabers)"}," feat and loses ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Pistols)"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Sith Weaponmaster"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Sith pride themselves on aggression. They believe they can defeat an opponent no matter what weapon they face or how and when they are attacked. DE Training Droids that fall into Sith hands are often turned into something a half step removed from an Assassin Droid. They are armed with a variety of weapons and reprogrammed to strike at their masters at any time without notice. Although the Droids rarely succeed, they do their duty with the unshakable tenacity that only a machine can muster.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["To modify a Duelist Elite in this manner, begin by removing its programming safeguards, which requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check against the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},". If the check is successful, the Droid will no longer stop automatically when its opponent's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," fall to single digits. Next, reprogram the Droid to favor a specific type of weapon, which requires a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and 30 minutes of work. Finally, swap one or more of the Droid's current ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"}," for others. But beware: if the Droid is disabled or otherwise shuts down, it reverts to its original programming when restarted. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Modification: Stiletto Droid"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The nobility of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Tapani Sector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tapani_Sector?action=edit&redlink=1"}," settle their differences with duels. In addition to being educated and graceful, nobles are expected to be deadly with a blade, and they have discovered a way for the Droid to play a part in the intrigues of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tapani Nobility"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tapani_Nobility","referenceId":"reference:116393e4f9b4af65"},". Turning the Duelist Elite into an outright assassin would be considered bad form, but giving the Droid a few weapons that might kill a rival \"accidentally\" during practice is business as usual. A few nobles keep these so-called Stiletto Droids around on purpose to prove that they can handle any threat that comes their way.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The modification begins with programming a hidden command into the Droid, which requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check against the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"}," and 30 minutes of work. (Erasing the command trail that leads back to the programmer increases the check DC by 10.) If the modification is successful, the Droid is programmed to reveal and use a hidden weapon on a specific signal, such as a dropped handkerchief or a spoken keyword. This signal can also be an action taken by the intended target, such as lowering a weapon or turning his or her back on the Droid. Next, install a weapon, such as a small knife or blaster, somewhere in the Droid, usually concealed within the arm or torso. This installation requires a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and 1 hour of work. Detecting the weapon requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check against the result of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check made to install it or against the Droid's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},", whichever is higher. The first time the Droid makes an attack with this weapon, it does so as if its target is ",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},". \n"]},"\n","\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["DE Training Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n","Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["4th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/4th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 1\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +7; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 15, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 11\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 30, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Immune:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Traits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Traits"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," 6 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Walking"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Walking","referenceId":"reference:1dabd5131fa6e9e4"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Melee:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","chil